        "description": "<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/9e589119-8308-4809-9b3b-2a940b5bf9fe,1774298385310/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C212%2C3512%2C1975%29%3BResize%3D%28620%29' alt='A line of vans is seen in a parking lot.' width='620' height='349' title='About 38,000 rides have been provided through the Sioux Lookout First Nations Health Authority&apos;s medical transportation program in Thunder Bay, Ont., since April 2024.'/><p>The Sioux Lookout First Nations Health Authority (SLFNHA) has announced it is suspending its medical transportation program in Thunder Bay, Ont., due to a lack of funding from Indigenous Services Canada and the Non-Insured Health Benefits program. Here's what the change means for people who rely on the service and the more than 20 staff members who have been laid off.</p>",
