        "description": "<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/0b6cf587-da22-46c4-aa72-bb2fc6e6c6da,1773923248401/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C27%2C2000%2C1125%29%3BResize%3D%28620%29' alt='A man and a woman examine documents at a desk.' width='620' height='349' title='Doreen Manuel and Brett Forester, right, examine documents on the RCMP&apos;s surveillance of Indigenous leaders during the 1970s.'/><p>Today, we begin publishing a series of exclusive stories that expose a sweeping RCMP program of surveillance, disruption and infiltration of Indigenous organizations between 1968 and 1982. Though long suspected by Indigenous leaders across Canada, the scope and scale of the spy program has remained hidden behind walls of government secrecy, until now.\n</p>",
